{
  "id": "Compound::DB00663 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Flumethasone Pivalate, a glucocorticoid, is shown to bind to Serpina6, which is then bound by various glucocorticoids, including Alclometasone, Halobetasol Propionate, and Rimexolone. All these compounds share a common pathway leading to the receptor Nr3c1, a key component of the glucocorticoid receptor signaling pathway. The lowest common ancestors of these glucocorticoids are consistently linked to the class of therapeutic glucocorticoids and 20-oxo steroids, reinforcing their shared biological role. The evidence suggests that Flumethasone Pivalate, through its interaction with Serpina6, may indirectly influence Nr3c1 via a glucocorticoid-mediated signaling cascade. The recurring involvement of glucocorticoid receptors and the shared pathway indicate a potential mechanism where Flumethasone Pivalate could act as a modulator of Nr3c1 activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
